<title>INDIA: Bank of India begins trading on BSE.</title>
<headline>Bank of India begins trading on BSE.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of newly-listed Bank of India began trading on the Bombay bourse on Monday and were quoted at 59.50 rupees minutes after opening against an issue price of 45 rupees, traders said.  </p>
<p>The state-run bank raised 6.75 billion rupees in February through an inital public offering of equity.</p>
<p>Bank of India said last week its net profit for the year ended March 31, 1997 rose to 4.48 billion rupees from 2.76 billion a year ago.</p>
<p>The shares are also due to begin trading on the National and Ahmedabad bourses this week.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
